Object ( Variant Q, Bit ClkG, Bit Done
    , Bit Busy) RegisterDepth( Variant D, Bit ClkG, Variant Depth
    , Bit Go, Bit Wait) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Shifters\\Advanced"
{
 // Same as RegDepth except with a GDBW model
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Variant D:	The value to be registered on the next rising clock edge if Go is high and Busy is low.
 //
 // Bit ClkG:	The clock for the operation.  If disconnected, defaults to ClkG, the global user clock signal.
 //
 // Bit Go:	The Go of GDBW.  Enables the latching of the input data, as long as not Busy.
 //
 // Bit Wait:	The Wait of GDBW.  If disconnected, defaults to a value of 0.  Holds off the Done.
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Variant Q:	The value in the last register of the register chain.
 //
 // Bit ClkG:	Clock input pass through
 //
 // Bit Done:	The Done of GDBW.  Indicates valid output Data.
 //
 // Bit Busy:	The Busy of GDBW.  Holds off the Go.
