Object ( Bit CO, Bit OFL, Variant Count) UpDownCount
    ( Variant CBy, Variant Init, Bit ClkG, Bit EN
    , Bit CLR, Bit Up, Bit CI, Bit InitEn) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Controllers\\Advanced",Documentation="with Init"
{
 // This is an up/down counter with additional Init inputs and an OFL output. Larger counters at higher frequencies may have difficulty passing timing specifications.
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Var/List CBy: Count by.  The dataset of CBy determines the size of the internal accumulator.  The value of CBy is what is added when EN is high.  CBy can have a different value each time EN is high.  If CBy is a List of Variants the counters have a nested behavior such that a roll over of one will increment the next most significant counter in the list.
 //
 // Var/List Init: The value to set the counter on InitEn.  Must be the same dataset as CBy.
 //
 // Bit ClkG: Global clock if disconnected or a specific clock if connected
 //
 // Bit EN: Enables the count.  If disconnected defaults to 1.
 //
 // Bit CLR: Asynchronous clear.  Clears all of the counters.  If disconnected defaults to 0.
 //
 // Bit Up: A value of 1 counts up (adds CBy).  A value of 0 counts down (subtracts CBy). If disconnected defaults to 1 (Up).
 //
 // Bit CI: The Carry In input for the least significant bit of the counter. Used for daisy chaining these counters together.  If you are not daisy chaining, then connect this input to an inverted value of the Up input.  If disconnected defaults to 0.
 //
 // Bit InitEn: This synchronous enable initializes the counters to the value of Init.  InitEn has precedence over EN.  If disconnected defaults to 0.
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Bit CO: Carry Out bit.  If the internal accumulator rolls over (or not under), this bit goes high.
 //
 // Bit OFL: Overflow bit.  If the internal accumulator overflows (or not underunderflows), this bit goes high.
 //
 // Var/List Count: Count output(s).  The result of the count.  This is the output of the internal accumulator register.  This output has the same dataset as CBy.
 //
 // Dataset Coverage:
 //
 // MSBxxx, LSBxxx, BINxxx (for unsigned use CO, for twos complement use OFL), Signed (use OFL), Fixed (use OFL) and List
 //
 // Revision 1
 //_ Object Prototypes
 Object ( Variant CBy) Input;  //_GUI 7,33
 Object ( Variant Init) Input:A;  //_GUI 7,42
 Object ( Bit ClkG) Input:B;  //_GUI 8,50
 //_ Attributes Resource="Global"
 Object ( Bit EN) Input:C;  //_GUI 8,53
 //_ Attributes Constant="1"
 Object ( Bit CLR) Input:D;  //_GUI 8,56
 //_ Attributes Constant="0"
 Object ( Bit Up) Input:E;  //_GUI 8,61
 //_ Attributes Constant="1"
 Object ( Bit CI) Input:F;  //_GUI 8,64
 //_ Attributes Constant="0"
 Object ( Bit InitEn) Input:G;  //_GUI 7,68
 //_ Attributes Constant="0"
 Object Output( Bit CO) ;  //_GUI 159,12
 Object Output:A( Bit OFL) ;  //_GUI 159,15
 Object Output:B( Variant Count) ;  //_GUI 131,32
 Object ( Variant Out1) Cast( Variant Type, Variant Data) ;  //_GUI 36,23
 Object ( Variant Out1, Variant Out2, Variant Out3) Junction
    ( Variant In0) ;  //_GUI 114,34
