Object ( Variant DataOut, Bit ClkG, Bit AClr
    , Bit Done, Bit Busy) Queue( Variant DataIn, Variant Size
    , Bit ClkG, Bit AClr, Bit Go, Bit Wait) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Memory",Documentation="var/bit"
{
 // A FIFO queue supporting a single clock domain.  Utilizes the standard GDBW protocol.  Same as the FIFO object except only supports one clock domain.
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Var/List DataIn: The data to be queued.
 //
 // Var/List Size: A dataset of N bits will produce a queue size of (2^N)-1 elements.
 //
 // Bit ClkG: The clock for the queue.  If disconnected, defaults to the ClkG, the global user clock signal.
 //
 // Bit Reset:	An synchronous reset for the queue.  Resets counters, not memory contents.
 //
 // Bit/List Go: Go of the GDBW protocol.  A
 // list of GOs will produce a list of independent queues.
 //
 // Bit/List Wait: Wait of the GDBW protocol.  If a list, must match GO.
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Var/List DataOut: Data coming out of the queue.  Is valid while Done is high.
 //
 // Var/List Count: Number of elements in the Queue read to be read.  Is valid while Done is high.
 //
 // Bit/List Done: Done of the GDBW protocol.  High when DataOut is valid.
 //
 // Bit/List Busy: Busy of the GDBW protocol.  Tells upstream not to Go.
 //
 // Revision 1
 //_ Object Prototypes
 Object ( Variant DataIn) Input;  //_GUI 35,24
 Object ( Variant Size) Input:A;  //_GUI 35,32
 Object ( Bit ClkG) Input:B;  //_GUI 35,43
 //_ Attributes Resource="Global"
