Object ( Variant RdData, Variant WrRdyCnt, Bit WrBsy
    , Bit WrAlmBsy, Bit WrErr, Variant FchRdyCnt, Bit FchBsy
    , Bit FchAlmBsy, Bit FchErr, Variant RetRdyCnt, Bit RetBsy
    , Bit RetAlmBsy, Bit RetErr) FIFO_Fetch_Retire( Variant WrData, Variant AddrBits
    , Variant BsyBits, Bit WrClk, Bit WrEn, Bit RdClk
    , Bit FchEn, Bit RetEn, Bit SyncFetch, Bit Clr) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Memory\\Advanced"
{
 // This FIFO allows the write side and the read side to be in different clock domains.
 //
 // A fetch retrieves the data from memory, but doesn't consume it.  A retire consumes the data but doesn't fetch it.  So fetch is followed by retire.  You can fetch past the end of your data as long as you don't retire past the end of your data.  To bring the fetch back to the retire point you need to trigger SyncFetch.
 //
 // This object is useful in situations where data must be prefetched before it is known whether or not it will actually be used, such as feeding data to the PCIX bus.
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Var WriteData:	Write data (ClkWr domain)
 // Var AddrBits:	The bitwidth of the data type defines the size of the memory allocated (2^AddrBits - 1 elements)
 // Var BsyBits:	The bitwidth of the data type defines the size of the memory allocated (2^AddrBits - 1 elements)
 // Bit WrClk:	Write clock
 // Bit WrEn:	Write Enable (ClkWr domain)
 // Bit RdClk:	Read clock
 // Bit FchEn:	Enables the fetch (read) of the the data without consuming it. (RdClk domain)
 // Bit RetEn:	Enables the retire of the data. (RdClk domain)
 // Bit SyncFetch:	Synchronize fetch pointer with retire pointer. (RdClk domain)
 // Bit Clr:	Clears the FIFO and any errors.  If disconnected, defaults to 0.
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Var RdData:	Read data.  Available after the FetchEn is clocked in. (RdClk domain)
 // Var WrRdyCnt:	the number of free elements ready to be written into (ClkWr domain)
 // Bit WrBsy:	The FIFO is full (ClkWr domain)
 // Bit WrAlmBsy:	The FIFO is almost full (2^BusyBits - 1 from full) (ClkWr domain)
 // Bit WrErr:	A write was performed while the FIFO was full - must CLR (ClkWr domain)
 // Var FchRdyCnt:	The number of elements ready to be fetched (RdClk domain)
 // Bit FchBsy:	There are no more elements to be fetched. (RdClk domain)
 // Bit FchAlmBsy:	The FIFO is almost empty (2^BusyBits - 1 elements left to fetch) (RdClk domain)
 // Bit FchErr:	A fetch was performed when there was no more data to be fetched.  You are allowed to fetch past the end of your data (you get undefined data) as long as you don't retire past the end of the data.  If you do fetch past the end of your data and haven't retired past the end of your data, this error is cleared when the fetch is synchronized. (RdClk domain)
 // Var RetRdyCnt:	The number of elements ready to be retired (RdClk domain)
 // Bit RetBsy:	There are no more elements to be retired. (RdClk domain)
 // Bit RetAlmBsy:	The FIFO is almost empty (2^BusyBits - 1 elements left to retire) (RdClk domain)
 // Bit RetErr:	A retire was performed when there was no more data to be retired.  The FIFO is now in an invalid state and must be cleared (Clr) before it can be used again. (RdClk domain)
 //
 // Revision 1
 //_ Object Prototypes
