 Object Text;  //_GUI 211,239,Retiring when we don't have anything to retire is an error.
 Object Text;  //_GUI 315,161,Here we have to detect another type of error.  There is a time between a fetch with an error and when it is retired.  If between that time another value is written into the FIFO, the error detection logic to the left (AND of RetireBusy and Retire) will not detect the error.  Any errored fetch should produce a retire error when that value is retired.  This is explained in #2 below.And one more error:  If there is valid data to fetch, but the retire gets ahead of the fetch.  This is explained in #1 below.
