Object ( Variant OFL, Variant Q, Bit ClkG
    , Bit AClr, Bit Done, Variant Busy) Div( Variant N
    , Variant D, Bit ClkG, Bit AClr, Variant Go
    , Bit Wait) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\ArithmeticOps",Icon="DIV"
{
 // Synchronous divide.  GDBW behavior with synchronizing input queues.
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Variant N: Dividend or Numerator
 //
 // Variant D: Divisor or Denominator
 //
 // Bit ClkG: Global clock if disconnected or a specific clock if connected
 //
 // Bit AClr: Asynchronous clear.  Has a value of 0 if disconnected
 //
 // Bit/List Go: Go
 //
 // Bit Wait: Wait. Defaults to 0 if disconnected.
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Variant OFL: Overflow or Error.  List if N or D are Lists, otherwise Bit.
 //
 // Variant Q: Quotient.  List if N or D are Lists.
 //
 // Bit ClkG: clock input pass through
 //
 // Bit AClr: clear input pass through
 //
 // Bit Done: Done
 //
 // Bit/List Busy: Busy
 //
 // Dataset Coverage:
 //
 // MSBxxx, LSBxxx and BINxxx (unsigned,  Q is the same dataset as N and D symmetrized,  Q is not rounded), Signed (Q is the same dataset as N and D symmetrized,  Q is not rounded but truncated towards negative infinity), Floating (infinity and NaN supported, Q is the same dataset as N and D symmetrized), Fixed (the size of whole and fractional portions of Q are each  the total number of bits for N or D symmetrized) and one or two Lists.  Complex is not supported. N and D are symmetrized and a warning is produced if they are different sizes.  N and D cannot have mixed datasets except for MSB, LSB and BIN.
 //
 // Revision 1
