//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Shifters"
{
 // Serial to Parallel with clear, a space to time converter.
 //
 // INPUTS:
 // S_Data: Serial data latched when Go is high and Busy is low.
 //
 // P_Type: The data type of the P_Data output.  If the size of S_Data doesn't divide evenly into the size of P_Type a warning is produced and the remainder bits are zero extended and output in the last stage.
 //
 // ClkG: The ClkG global clock, if not connected.  Otherwise any other clock.  This object has been tested up to 200 MHz.
 //
 // AClr: An asynchronous clear. If unconnected, defaults to the global asynchronous clear.
 //
 // Go: When high and Busy is low, S_Data is registered.
 //
 // Wait: When high, Done will stay low.  The down-stream object raises the Wait signal if it is not ready for data.
 //
 // OUTPUTS:
 // P_Data: The parallel output data is valid when Done is high.
 //
 // Done: Indicates when valid parallel data is coming out of P_Data to be registered.  Done will never go high while Wait is high
 //
 // Busy: Indicates when Go and associated data will be ignored.  (Proper protocol is that Go should drop if Busy goes high.)
 //
 // Revision 1
