Object ( Variant Data, Variant In_Type, Variant StageMsk
    , Bit Done, Bit Busy) PToS_Or_SToP( Variant Data, Variant Out_Type
    , Bit ClkG, Bit AClr, Bit Go, Bit Wait) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Shifters\\Advanced"
{
 // Does a ParallelToSerial or a SerialToParallel (or passthrough) based upon the data sizes of Data and Out_Type.
 //
 // See Parallel->Serial_Clr and Serial->Parallel_Clr for more info.
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Variant Data: The input data that will be serialized or deserialized.
 //
 // Variant Out_Type: The dataset of the output data that was deserialized or serialized.
 //
 // Bit ClkG: The clock for the operation.  If disconnected, defaults to ClkG, the global user clock signal.
 //
 // Bit AClr: Asynchronously clears the register.  If disconnected, defaults to 0.
 //
 // Bit Go: The Go of GDBW.  Enables the latching of the input data, as long as not Busy.
 //
 // Bit Wait: The Wait of GDBW.  If disconnected, defaults to a value of 0.  Holds off the Done.
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Variant Data: The output Data that was deserialized or serialized.
 //
 // Variant In_Type: The dataset of the input data.
 //
 // Variant StageMsk: This is a walking-one mask that indicates what stage of the PtoS or StoP conversion we are in.  One bit per stage and the enabled bit walks from LSB to MSB.
 //
 // Bit Done: The Done of GDBW.  Indicates valid output Data.
 //
 // Bit Busy: The Busy of GDBW.  Holds off the Go.
 //
 // Revision 1
 //_ Object Prototypes
 Object ( Variant Data) Input;  //_GUI 16,25
