Object ( Variant Data, Variant Count, Bit Full
    , Bit Empty) Stack( Variant Data, Variant Size, Bit "Push/Pop"
    , Bit ClkG, Bit En, Bit AClr) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Memory\\Advanced",Documentation="En"
{
 // Stack
 //
 // To Push, if Full isn't high, raise En and lower Push/Pop for one clock cycle along with valid data on Data.
 //
 // To Pop, if Empty isn't high, raise En and Push/Pop, and on the following clock cycle, valid data is available on Data.
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Data - Data to be pushed onto the stack.
 //
 // Size - The dataset represents the number of bits used for the stack's internal memory address space. For instance a Size of MSB003 would produce a maximum stack size of 8 elements.
 //
 // Push/Pop - Push = 0, Pop = 1.  Combine with En to push or pop.
 //
 // ClkG - The clock input.  If left disconnected, defaults to the global symbol ClkG.
 //
 // En - Enable the Stack object to push or pop depending upon the Push/Pop input.  If a push is attempted while the stack is full or a pop is attempted while the stack is empty, the funtion is not performed and the state of the stack object is mantained.
 //
 // AClr - Asynchronous clear.  Clears the stack pointers and count, but doesn't clear the stack memory.
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Data - Data that has been Popped. Valid after the rising click edge with En high, Push/Pop high, and Empty low.
 //
 // Count - Current number of elements in Stack
 //
 // Empty - Boolean
 //
 // Full - Boolean
 //
 // There is also a GDBW version of Stack in CoreLib.
 //
 // Revision 1
 //_ Object Prototypes
 Object ( Variant Data) Input;  //_GUI 29,25
 Object ( Variant Size) Input:A;  //_GUI 12,75
 Object ( Bit "Push/Pop") Input:B;  //_GUI 12,101
 //_ Attributes Documentation="Push=0",Pop="1"
 Object ( Bit ClkG) Input:C;  //_GUI 12,116
 //_ Attributes Resource="Global"
 Object ( Bit En) Input:D;  //_GUI 16,161
