Object ( Variant Data, Variant Count, Bit Full
    , Bit Empty, Bit Done, Bit Busy) Stack( Variant Data
    , Variant Size, Bit ClkG, Bit AClr, Bit Go
    , Bit Wait) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Memory",Go="Push",Wait="Don't Pop"
{
 // A GDBW (Go/Done/Busy/Wait) based Stack object.
 //
 // To Push, if Busy isn't high, raise Go for one clock cycle along with valid data on Data.
 //
 // To Pop, drop Wait for one clock cycle, and if there is valid data, Done will rise along with valid data on Data.
 //
 // Popping and pushing are independent and can happen simultaneously in which case the data is passed through in the same cycle.
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Data - Data to be pushed onto the stack.
 //
 // Size - A dataset of N bits will produce a stack size of (2^N)-1 elements.
 //
 // ClkG - The clock input.  If left disconnected, defaults to the global symbol ClkG.
 //
 // AClr - Asynchronous clear.  Clears the stack pointers and count, but doesn't clear the stack memory.
 //
 // Go - Push Data if not Busy
 //
 // Wait - a.k.a. Don't Pop.  When it is low, it means "You can pop if there is data," or "Don't wait for me, baby. Gi'me what you got."
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Data - Popped data.  Only valid when Done is high. Will have undefined values when Done is low.
 //
 // Count - The number of elements on the stack.  The dataset is the same size as the Size input.
 //
 // Full - High when the stack becomes full. Note that you can still push data while the stack is full as long as the output is not waiting.  In that case the data is passed through and never put into memory.  Basically this output is for information only and you should use Busy to decide whether or not to push data.
 //
 // Empty - High when the stack becomes empty. Note that you can still pop data while the stack is empty as long as the Wait input is low when the Go input is high.  In that case the data is passed through and never put into memory.  Basically this output is for information only and you should use Wait to hold off any pops and Done to latched popped data.
 //
 // Done - Indicates popped data is valid on the Data output.  Will only go high if Wait is low and there is data to pop.
 //
 // Busy - Indicates if the stack is full and the output is Waiting.  Note that Busy will be low and you can still push if the stack is full as long as there is a simultaneous pop (not Wait) because the data just passes through to the pop without storing on the stack.
 //
 // There is also a non-GDBW version of Stack in the Advanced branch of this tree.
 //
 // Revision 1
 //_ Object Prototypes
 Object ( Variant Data) Input;  //_GUI 7,12
 Object ( Variant Size) Input:A;  //_GUI 7,25
 Object ( Bit ClkG) Input:B;  //_GUI 7,28
 //_ Attributes Resource="Global"
 Object ( Bit AClr) Input:C;  //_GUI 7,35
 //_ Attributes Constant="0"
 Object ( Bit Go) Input:D;  //_GUI 7,128
 Object ( Bit Wait) Input:E;  //_GUI 182,179
 Object Output( Variant Data) ;  //_GUI 238,95
 Object Output:A( Variant Count) ;  //_GUI 232,117
 Object Output:B( Bit Full) ;  //_GUI 232,120
 Object Output:C( Bit Empty) ;  //_GUI 232,123
 Object Output:D( Bit Done) ;  //_GUI 186,138
 Object Output:E( Bit Busy) ;  //_GUI 16,189
 Object ( Bit Out) INVERT( Bit In1) ;  //_GUI 21,129
 Object ( Bit Out) AND( Bit In1, Bit In2) ;  //_GUI 33,127
 Object ( Bit Out) INVERT:A( Bit In1) ;  //_GUI 158,138
 Object ( Bit Out) AND:A( Bit In1, Bit In2) ;  //_GUI 170,136
 Object ( Variant Out1) XOR( Variant In1, Variant In2) ;  //_GUI 51,80
 Object ( Variant Data) RAMSP( Variant Data, Variant Addr
    , Bit ClkG, Bit WE) ;  //_GUI 188,91
 Object ( Variant State) State( Variant Enter, Variant Leave
    , Bit ClkG, Bit CLR) ;  //_GUI 121,135
 Object ( Bit Out) AND:B( Bit In1, Bit In2) ;  //_GUI 99,137
 Object ( Bit Out1) EqualAllOnes( Variant In1) ;  //_GUI 91,167
 Object Text;  //_GUI 123,130,HaveData
 Object Text;  //_GUI 159,145,Done while HaveData and not Waiting
 Object Text;  //_GUI 30,135,Go1 When Go and not Busy
 Object Text;  //_GUI 85,149,Enter HaveData when Go1.Leave HaveData when one left and done (if simultaniously Go1 then Leave is overridden by Enter)
