Object ( Variant Iteration, Bit LastDone, Bit Active
    , Bit Done, Bit Busy) DoneForN_Up( Variant Iterations, Bit ClkG
    , Bit CLR, Bit Go, Bit Wait) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Controllers\\Advanced"
{
 // Produces N Dones for every one Go.  Outputs the Done iteration count incrementing from 0 to N-1. Uses the standard GDBW model.  Larger iterations at higher frequencies may have difficulty passing timing specifications.
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Var/List Iterations: This value indicates the number of iterations or Dones to produce for every Go.  A Go with an Iterations value of 0 will produce no Done at all.  Iterations can be a list which yields nested loops, each loop with its own Iteration, LastDone, Active and Done.  The least significant element in Iterations is the inner loop.
 //
 // Bit ClkG: Global clock if disconnected or a specific clock if connected
 //
 // Bit Go: Start producing N Dones.
 //
 // Bit Wait: Wait. Has a value of 0 if disconnected.  Holds off the Dones
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Var/List Iteration The Done iteration value.  Same dataset as the Iterations input.  Values only valid while Done is high.  The first Done iteration value is 0. the LastDone iteration value is N-1.
 //
 // Bit/List LastDone Indicates when the last Done is occurring.
 //
 // Bit/List Active: Same behavior as the Done signal except it does not drop during Wait.
 //
 // Bit/List Done: N of these are produced for every Go.
 //
 // Bit Busy: Tells Go to hold off.
 //
 // Dataset Coverage:
 //
 // MSBxxx, LSBxxx and BINxxx
 //
 // Revision 2: allow for change of Iterations to 1 while still running the previous loop
 //
 // Documentation for List overload added.
 //_ Object Prototypes
 Object ( Variant Iterations) Input;  //_GUI 13,16
 Object ( Bit ClkG) Input:A;  //_GUI 13,114
 //_ Attributes Resource="Global"
 Object ( Bit CLR) Input:B;  //_GUI 13,117
 //_ Attributes Constant="0"
 Object ( Bit Go) Input:C;  //_GUI 13,126
 Object ( Bit Wait) Input:D;  //_GUI 214,131
 //_ Attributes Constant="0"
 Object Output( Variant Iteration) ;  //_GUI 216,15
 Object Output:A( Bit LastDone) ;  //_GUI 216,64
 Object Output:B( Bit Active) ;  //_GUI 221,92
 Object Output:C( Bit Done) ;  //_GUI 216,110
 Object Output:D( Bit Busy) ;  //_GUI 150,153
 Object ( Bit Out1) VouchBit( Variant In1) ;  //_GUI 78,107
