Object ( Variant OFL, Variant Q, Bit ClkG
    , Bit AClr, Bit Done, Bit Busy) ConvertList( Variant Type
    , List Data, Bit ClkG, Bit AClr, Bit Go
    , Bit Wait) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\Converters\\Advanced",Documentation="var/list"
{
 // Converts elements in a List to the Type input.  If The Data input is a List and the Type is some known type other than List, every element in the Data List will be converted to the known type.  If the type input is also a List, however, this object will decompose the Type and Data Lists in parallel until a non-List type is reached on the Type input.  The remaining elements in the Data List will then each be converted to this Type.  The number of elements in the Data List must be >= number of elements in the Type List and must be shape-compatible or undefined behavior will result.  The only difference between ConvertList(6,6) and Convert(6,6) is ConvertList(6,6) has a bit or a list of bits for OFL that match the list shape of the input Data.  Convert(6,6) always has a bit OFL even with List inputs. For more information on supported dataset conversions see Convert(6,6).
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Var/List Type: The destination dataset(s) for the conversion.
 //
 // Var/List Data: The value(s) to be converted.
 //
 // Bit ClkG: Global clock if disconnected or a specific clock if connected
 //
 // Bit AClr: Asynchronous clear.  Clears all of the counters.  If disconnected defaults to 0.
 //
 // Bit Go: Go
 //
 // Bit Wait: Wait. Has a value of 0 if disconnected
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Bit/List OFL: Indicates that there was an overflow in the conversion (shrinking) of
 // the dataset: One OFL bit per Data list element.
 //
 // Var/List output: The results of Data being converted to Type.
 //
 // Bit ClkG: clock input pass through
 //
 // Bit AClr: Clear input pass through
 //
 // Bit Done: Done
 //
 // Bit Busy: Busy
 //
 // Revision 1
 //_ Object Prototypes
 Object ( Variant Type) Input;  //_GUI 44,27
 Object ( List Data) Input:A;  //_GUI 44,30
 Object ( Bit ClkG) Input:B;  //_GUI 44,33
 //_ Attributes Resource="Global"
 Object ( Bit AClr) Input:C;  //_GUI 44,36
 //_ Attributes Constant="0"
 Object ( Bit Go) Input:D;  //_GUI 44,42
 Object ( Bit Wait) Input:E;  //_GUI 64,50
 //_ Attributes Constant="0"
 Object Output( Variant OFL) ;  //_GUI 66,27
 Object Output:A( Variant Q) ;  //_GUI 66,30
 Object Output:B( Bit ClkG) ;  //_GUI 66,36
 Object Output:C( Bit AClr) ;  //_GUI 66,39
 Object Output:D( Bit Done) ;  //_GUI 66,42
 Object Output:E( Bit Busy) ;  //_GUI 46,50
 Object ( Variant OFL, Variant Q, Variant PipeLen
    , Bit ClkG, Bit AClr, Bit Done, Bit Busy) Convert_Pipe
    ( Variant Type, Variant Data, Bit ClkG, Bit AClr
    , Bit Go, Bit Wait) ;  //_GUI 50,26
 //_ Attributes Documentation="Floating->Signed"
 Object Text;  //_GUI 37,57,Covers the Var/List and the List/List cases.

 //_ Behavior Topology
 Output.0 = Convert_Pipe.0;  
 Output:A.0 = Convert_Pipe.1;  
 Output:B.0 = Convert_Pipe.3;  
 Output:C.0 = Convert_Pipe.4;  
 Output:D.0 = Convert_Pipe.5;  
 Output:E.0 = Convert_Pipe.6;  //_GUI 46,46
 Convert_Pipe.0 = Input.0;  
