Object ( Variant OFL, Variant Neg, Bit ClkG
    , Bit AClr, Bit Done, Variant Busy) Negate( Variant Val
    , Bit ClkG, Bit AClr, Variant Go, Bit Wait) 
//_ Attributes TreeGroup="CoreLib\\ArithmeticOps"
{
 // A synchronous negate object.
 //
 // Inputs:
 //
 // Var/List Val: A value or a list of values that will be negated.
 //
 // Bit ClkG: Global clock if disconnected or a specific clock if connected
 //
 // Bit AClr: Asynchronous clear.  Has a value of 0 if disconnected
 //
 // Bit/List Go: Go of GDBW.  Can have a list of Goes (one Go per Val) if want to synchronize all Vals.
 //
 // Bit Wait: Wait of GDBW.  If disconnected, has value of 0.
 //
 // Outputs:
 //
 // Bit/List OFL: Indicates there was an overflow in the negation.  A list if Val is a list, or a Bit otherwise
 //
 // Var/List Neg: The result of the negate operation.  A list if Val is a list.
 //
 // Bit ClkG: Clock input pass through
 //
 // Bit AClr: Clear input pass through
 //
 // Bit Done: Done of GDBW
 //
 // Bit/List Busy: Busy of GDBW.  One Busy per Go.
 //
 // Dataset Coverage:
 //
 // MSBxxx, LSBxxx and BINxxx (will treat as twos complement and will produce a warning), Signed, Fixed, Floating, Complex and lists of these.
 //
 // Revision 1
 //_ Object Prototypes
 Object ( Variant Val) Input;  //_GUI 27,29
 Object ( Bit ClkG) Input:A;  //_GUI 43,35
