 Object Text;  //_GUI 132,143,In the case where both datasets are too big, we have two different algorithms that will work: $Karat_Pipe and $Mult_Pipe_SplitAB.  $Karat_Pipe uses 3 multipliers per recursion stage but has a longer pipeline length.  $MULT_Pipe_SplitAB uses 4 multipliers per pipeline stage but has a shorter pipeline length. usually $Karat_Pipe uses less multipliers, but in some cases $Mult_Pipe_SplitAB uses less because in the $Karat_Pipe implementation, after the dataset split occurs, there is an add before the multiply which increases the split dataset by one bit.
