 Object Text;  //_GUI 4,52,This object creates LSB lists of all the possible left shifts for a dataset.It's true: this object is a bit of a mystery, but here's the basic plan. We pop bits off of the left side of our incoming data and pad the right side of the remaining data with zeros. This is our standard shift. The falloff data is built from the popped-off data.
